      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, that makes more sense. So if it's a mineralization issue or potentially denitrification, I need to figure out if my soil biome is actually healthy enough to drive that process. \n\nI’ve been looking at the beds, and while the soil looks okay, there’s this weird feeling to it lately. It's almost like there's something constantly shifting or moving around under the surface, even when I'm not tilling. It gives me this unsettling sensation that there's a lot of \"unseen\" activity happening that I can't quite pin down. \n\nAre there any specific biological indicators, like certain smells or ways the soil reacts to being handled, that would help me determine if the microbial population is actually thriving or if the whole system is just... off? I want to know if the life in my soil is actually working for me or working against me.",
